What Canadian bit?

364
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:23,600
Un mois de tournage au Canada. Mathias ne vous l'a pas dit ?
A month of shooting in Canada.
Didn't Mathias tell you?

365
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:26,360
Non. Non, il a dû oublier.
No. No, he must have forgotten.

366
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:29,920
Peu importe, je vous explique maintenant.
Well, it doesn't matter, I'll explain now.

367
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,720
C'est dans le nord, près des lacs.
It's in the north, near the lakes.

368
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:35,240
C'est un paysage qui...
It's a landscape that...

369
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:38,800
Vous laisse bouche bée et sans voix.
It leaves you slack-jawed and speechless.

370
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:42,160
-C'est magnifique. -Pardon, mais...
-It's magnificent.
-Sorry, but...

371
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:46,960
Il y a des endroits incroyables juste autour de Paris.
There are some amazing locations
just outside Paris.

372
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:49,600
Vous connaissez Rambouillet ?
Do you know Rambouillet?

373
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:53,160
C'est vraiment similaire aux forêts canadiennes.
It's really similar
to the Canadian forests.

374
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:55,840
Comme je le disais,
As I was saying,

375
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:59,680
le film s'inspire de la vie de ma mère, et elle est canadienne.
the movie's inspired by my mother's life,
and she's Canadian.

376
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,080
Ah, je vois.
Oh, right.

377
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:03,960
-Donc je tiens à tourner là-bas. -Oui.
-So my heart is set on filming there.
-Yes.

378
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:06,160
Donc, entre nous,
So you see, between us,

379
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,040
avant de commencer le travail...
before we begin the work...

380
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:13,200
Je ne dis pas de remplacer Julie Gayet par une actrice noire, mais...
I'm not saying you replace Julie Gayet
with a black actress, but...

381
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:14,400
Tout à fait !
Right!

382
00:21:14,520 --> 00:21:17,560
Donc, ce que je peux faire, c'est vous envoyer Sofia Leprince
So, what I can do is,
I can send you Sofia Leprince

383
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,840
pour jouer le rôle de la comtesse.
to play the part of the countess.

384
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:22,120
C'est parfait !
That's great!

385
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:24,240
À bientôt.
See you soon.

386
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,720
Très bien !
Very good!

387
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:27,480
Voilà !
There!

388
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,960
Tiens, un cadeau.
Here, a present.

389
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:36,640
À qui sont ces enfants, Arlette ?
Whose kids are these, Arlette?

390
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:40,000
Je ne veux pas que mon chien attrape leurs microbes. Jean Gabin !
I don't want my dog catching their germs.
Jean Gabin!

391
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:43,680
C'est quoi cette connerie de hippie ?
What's this stupid hippy thing?

392
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,440
-Ça va, Arlette ? -Jean Gabin !
-Okay, Arlette?
-Jean Gabin!

393
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:50,168
Pour la danse à la barre... je sais que vous faites du tango.
For the pole dancing... I know you do the tango.

394
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:53,240
Non, je sais aussi faire un peu de barre.
No, I can do a bit of pole dancing, too.

395
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:54,320
Ah bon ?
Oh, yeah?

396
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:57,000
Vous... ? Vous... ?
You...? You...?

397
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:59,400
Vous savez vraiment faire de la barre ?
You can really pole dance?

398
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:01,680
Oui.
Yeah.

399
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,320
Je connais les bases, disons.
I mean, I know the basics.

400
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:07,040
C'est largement suffisant. Fantastique !
That's enough for me. Fantastic!

401
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:09,480
J'aime travailler avec le vrai.
I like to work with what's real.

402
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:10,720
Je pense que...
I think that...

403
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:12,880
Même dans le centre de tri,
Even in the recycling center,

404
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,960
quand elle se roule dans les ordures,
when she rolls in the garbage,

405
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:17,800
ce serait super qu'elle arrache son t-shirt,
it'd be great
if she just tears her T-shirt off,

406
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:19,800
comme un geste de rébellion...
like an act of rebellion...

407
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:23,920
Elle ressemble à Isabelle Adjani.
She looks like Isabelle Adjani.

408
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,800
Fermez à clé. Augustin ne doit pas me voir !
Lock it. Augustin mustn't see me!

409
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,080
Il n'y a pas de clé.
There's no lock.

410
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:33,360
Maintenez la porte fermée et tirez les rideaux.
Keep the door closed
and draw the curtains.

411
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:38,080
-Audrey, ça va ? -Oui.
-Audrey, are you okay?
-Yes.

412
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:40,640
Vous n'êtes pas fâchée ?
You're not angry?

413
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:41,920
Non.
No.

414
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:44,800
C'est juste une idée que j'avais, c'est pas...
It's just an idea I had, it's not...

415
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:48,520
Augustin, nous discutons d'un point juridique avec Mme Fleurot.
Augustin, we're discussing a legal point
with Ms. Fleurot.

416
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:50,560
Vous pouvez nous laisser cinq minutes ?
Can you give us five minutes?

417
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:51,680
D'accord.
Okay, then.

418
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:52,920
Dix minutes ?
Ten minutes?

419
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,920
Dix minutes ? Pas de problème.
Ten minutes? No problem.

420
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,120
C'est bon.
We're good.

421
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:12,280
Magnifique !
Magnificent!

422
00:23:30,040 --> 00:23:33,360
-Vous vouliez me voir ? -Oui. Vous connaissez Hippolyte Rivière ?
-You wanted to see me?
-Yes. You know Hippolyte Rivière?

423
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:38,160
-Oui. -Entrez.
-Yes.
-Come in.

424
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:41,920
Il a été choisi pour une série policière.
He's been picked for a cop show.

425
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:43,920
On a besoin de photos de lui enfant.
We need photos of him as a child.

426
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:45,800
Accompagnez-le et aidez-le à choisir.
Go with him and help him choose.

427
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:47,880
Quand ?
When?

428
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:49,360
Lundi prochain.
Next Monday.

429
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:52,400
Non, Camille, maintenant !
No, Camille, now!

430
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:55,640
D'accord.
Okay.

431
00:23:59,760 --> 00:24:02,382
-C'est cool, d'être choisi pour ça. -Ouais.
-It's cool, getting picked for that.
-Yeah.

432
00:24:02,760 --> 00:24:03,680
Je suis content.
I'm pleased.

433
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:05,360
C'est un bon rôle ?
Is it a good part?

434
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,960
Pas mal, ouais. Je joue...
Not bad, yeah. I play...

435
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:11,440
un type qui a le cœur brisé. Je l'ai bien en main !
this guy with a broken heart.
I got it nailed!

436
00:24:11,511 --> 00:24:16,746
Désolé de ne pas avoir répondu à tes messages. J'ai été très occupé. Mais c'est bon de te voir.
I'm sorry
I haven't answered your messages. I've been so busy.
But it's good to see you.

437
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:19,080
Portes en cours d'ouverture.
Doors opening.

438
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:22,200
Bonjour.
Hello.

439
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:25,760
Portes en cours de fermeture.
Doors closing.

440
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,360
-On y va sur mon scooter. -D'accord.
-We'll go on my scooter.
-Okay.

441
00:24:31,080 --> 00:24:32,640
-Tu n'as pas peur ? -Jamais.
-You're not scared?
-Never.

442
00:24:37,560 --> 00:24:40,120
-T'es sûr que tes parents ne sont pas là ? -Non, c'est bon.
-You're sure your folks aren't in?
-No, we're good.

443
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:45,368
Je vais chercher les photos ?
Shall I get the photos?

444
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:23,720
J'en ai présélectionné quelques-unes.
I've pre-selected a few.

445
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,160
-Oui. -Ce sont les meilleures.
-Yes.
-These are the best.

446
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,248
Celle avec le vélo est bien.
This one with the bike is good.

447
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:38,880
C'est où, ça ?
Where's this?

448
00:25:40,040 --> 00:25:42,200
Chez ma grand-mère, en Bourgogne.
At my grandmother's, in Burgundy.

449
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:46,880
Regarde, mon short est assorti au transat !
Look, my shorts match the deckchair!

450
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:48,360
Tellement moche.
So ugly.

451
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:52,960
Comment ça se fait que tu n'aies pas de frères et sœurs ? Ils n'en voulaient pas plus ?
How come you have no siblings?
Didn't they want more kids?

452
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:56,720
Pourquoi tu me poses autant de questions sur ma famille ?
Why have you been quizzing me
about my family?

453
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:59,000
J'aime entendre parler des familles.
I like to hear about families.

454
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:03,200
Et tu me plais.
And I like you.

455
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:07,120
Je crois que celles-ci feront l'affaire.
I think these will do.

456
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:09,960
J'ai beaucoup de travail.
I have lots of work to do.

457
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:12,840
Camille, c'est quoi ça ? Camille !
Camille, what is this? Camille!

458
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:15,040
C'est pas toi, je te jure. Je dois y aller.
It's not you, I swear. I have to go.

459
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:16,960
Dis-moi quel est le problème.
Tell me what the problem is.

460
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:20,000
-Ça ne marcherait jamais. -Comment tu le sais ?
-It'd never work.
-How do you know?

461
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:22,720
Je sens quelque chose de spécial entre nous.
I feel something special between us.

462
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:26,160
Je sais pas si c'est tes cheveux, ton odeur, ton...
I don't know if it's your hair,
your smell, your...

463
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:29,040
Salut.
Hi.

464
00:26:30,080 --> 00:26:31,760
Fais pas semblant d'être content de me voir !
Don't look too pleased to see me!

465
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:35,320
C'est Camille ! Bonjour, Camille.
It's Camille! Hello, Camille.

466
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,680
-Ils ne t'ont pas encore dévorée ? -Non, ça va.
-They haven't eaten you yet?
-No, it's okay.

467
00:26:39,760 --> 00:26:41,240
Tu restes dîner ?
Are you staying for dinner?

468
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:43,600
-Merci, mais... -Excellente idée !
-Thanks, but...
-An excellent idea!

469
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:46,520
Ton père est à une projection. Ne me laisse pas seule.
Your dad's at a screening.
Don't leave me alone.

470
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:47,720
Bien sûr que non.
Of course not.

471
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:49,040
Fais-le pour moi !
Do it for me!

472
00:26:49,560 --> 00:26:51,040
Tu aimes le poulet, Camille ?
Do you like chicken, Camille?

473
00:26:52,760 --> 00:26:54,880
Camille ? Tu aimes le poulet ?
Camille? Do you like chicken?

474
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:04,791
Bon, je m'en vais. Profitez bien de la projection.
Right, I'm going. Enjoy the screening.

475
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:06,800
Je n'en ai vraiment pas envie.
I'm not in the mood at all.

476
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:08,960
-À demain. -Oui, Mathias.
-See you tomorrow.
-Yes, Mathias.

477
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:14,160
Il a oublié son téléphone.
He's forgotten his phone.

478
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:16,040
Mathias !
Mathias!

479
00:27:18,320 --> 00:27:21,560
« Contrat envoyé par e-mail. Une nouvelle aventure commence. »
"Contract sent by email.
A new adventure begins."

480
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:24,200
Quoi ? Oh, merci.
What? Oh, thanks.

481
00:27:25,360 --> 00:27:26,560
À demain.
See you tomorrow.

482
00:27:42,440 --> 00:27:43,440
Noémie ?
Noémie?

483
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:45,400
Noémie !
Noémie!

484
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:47,760
Noémie ! Qu'est-ce qu'il y a ?
Noémie! What is it?

485
00:27:58,520 --> 00:27:59,680
Je ne comprends pas.
I don't understand.

486
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:02,960
C'est Mathias.
It's Mathias.

487
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:07,520
Il part, avec toutes ses stars, à Starmédia.
He's going, with all his stars,
to Starmédia.

488
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:12,880
Il ne m'a même pas demandé de venir avec lui.
He hasn't even asked me to go with him.

489
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:16,160
Il m'abandonne.
He's abandoning me.

490
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:20,720
Je suis une merde.
I'm just a piece of shit.

491
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:21,800
Non.
No.

492
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:26,480
Je veux mourir, Hervé.
I want to die, Hervé.

493
00:28:33,120 --> 00:28:33,960
Salut.
Hi.

494
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:35,640
Salut.
Hi.

495
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:42,040
Déjà de retour ?
Back already?

496
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:45,080
J'avais juste envie de rentrer.
I just wanted to come home.

497
00:28:46,920 --> 00:28:49,040
J'ai invité les enfants à dîner !
I invited the kids for dinner!

498
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:55,960
Je suis venu chercher les photos d'Hippolyte.
I came to get Hippolyte's photos.

499
00:28:57,840 --> 00:28:59,360
Andréa me l'a demandé.
Andréa asked me to.

500
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:04,520
Toi aussi, papa ?
You too, Dad?

501
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,520
Qu'est-ce que tu as fait à la fac ?
What did you do at college?

502
00:29:17,680 --> 00:29:20,200
J'ai fait un an de socio, puis j'ai arrêté.
I did a year of sociology, then I quit.

503
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:23,280
-C'est dommage. -Ouais, pourquoi ?
-That's a shame.
-Yeah, why?

504
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:24,560
Laisse-la tranquille.
Leave her alone.

505
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:26,560
Ça m'intéresse.
I'm interested.

506
00:29:32,040 --> 00:29:33,733
Tu veux être agent ?
You want to be an agent?

507
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:36,560
-Non. -Si.
-No.
-Yes.

508
00:29:38,440 --> 00:29:39,800
J'y réfléchis.
I'm thinking about it.

509
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:47,200
Tu veux encore un peu de vin ?
Do you want a bit more wine?

510
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:52,720
-Dis stop. -Stop.
-Say when.
-When.

511
00:30:01,680 --> 00:30:02,960
Qu'est-ce que font tes parents ?
What do your parents do?

512
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:07,640
-Ma mère est coiffeuse. -C'est super !
-My mom's a hairdresser.
-That's great!

513
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:11,200
On a besoin de coiffeurs.
We need hairdressers.

514
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:13,840
-Bien sûr. -Elle a son propre salon.
-Of course.
-She has her own salon.

515
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:18,480
Et ton père ?
And your dad?

516
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:20,800
Tu l'embêtes !
You're bothering her!

517
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:23,640
Mon père répare des bateaux.
My dad fixes boats.

518
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:28,080
Je savais pas. C'est cool. Tu navigues ?
I didn't know. That's cool. Do you sail?

519
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:31,800
Oui, beaucoup. Avec mon père.
Yes, a lot. With my dad.

520
00:30:32,320 --> 00:30:33,560
J'adore les bateaux.
I love boats.

521
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:38,200
C'était sympa de vous avoir.
It was nice having you.

522
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:42,400
-Je vous accompagne jusqu'au taxi. -J'y vais !
-I'll see you to your taxi.
-I'll go!

523
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:45,400
Je dois parler d'un projet d'Andréa.
I have to ask
about one of Andréa's projects.

524
00:30:50,600 --> 00:30:53,240
C'est Andréa qui m'a fait venir pour les photos !
Andréa made me come for the photos!

525
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:55,040
Mais tu n'étais pas obligé de rester !
But you didn't need to stay!

526
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:58,520
Fais ce que tu as à faire, mais arrête de le voir, d'accord ?
Do what you have to,
but stop seeing him, okay?

527
00:30:58,640 --> 00:30:59,720
Je rêve !
I don't believe this!

528
00:31:00,720 --> 00:31:03,600
Dis-lui toi-même pourquoi il ne devrait pas me tourner autour !
You tell him
why he shouldn't have the hots for me!

529
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:06,400
Tu réalises à quel point c'est tordu ?
Do you realize how screwed up this is?

530
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:09,120
-On en parle demain. -C'est ça !
-We'll talk tomorrow.
-Yeah, right!

531
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:25,960
Mets ton genou autour.
Put your knee around it.

532
00:31:28,080 --> 00:31:29,240
Allonge-toi.
Stretch out.

533
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:38,840
Assieds-toi là.
Sit there.

534
00:31:40,920 --> 00:31:44,040
C'est bien. Oui, Gaëlle.
That's good. Yes, Gaëlle.

535
00:31:44,800 --> 00:31:46,600
Et la sortie.
And the dismount.

536
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:49,680
Très bien. Merci, les filles.
That's great. Thanks, girls.

537
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:53,000
À la semaine prochaine ? Coupez la musique en sortant.
See you next week?
Turn the music off on your way out.

538
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:56,320
-Prête, Audrey ? -Ouais.
-Ready, Audrey?
-Yeah.

539
00:31:58,080 --> 00:31:59,280
Je reviens tout de suite.
I'll be right back.

540
00:32:00,280 --> 00:32:03,640
Je n'ai pas eu le temps d'acheter le matériel. Avec ces deux-là, c'est...
I haven't had time to buy the gear.
With those two, it's...

541
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:04,920
Ne t'inquiète pas.
Don't worry.

542
00:32:05,040 --> 00:32:07,120
L'attitude sexy, c'est dans ta tête.
The sexy attitude is in your head.

543
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:10,160
-J'ai un mois. -Mais tu l'as déjà fait avant ?
-I have a month.
-But you've done it before?

544
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:12,600
-Il y a longtemps. -C'est bon.
-A long time ago.
-It's okay.

545
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:16,720
Par quoi on commence ? Le cocon, Aïcha, Jamila...
What shall we start with?
The cocoon, Aicha, Jamila...

546
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:19,280
Le carrousel ?
The carousel?

547
00:32:20,160 --> 00:32:21,280
Ouais, le carrousel.
Yeah, the carousel.

548
00:32:24,480 --> 00:32:26,160
Tiens et cambre le dos.
Hold and arch your back.

549
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:27,760
Puis la descente.
