-No...

726
00:43:19,480 --> 00:43:20,400
Si.
Yes.

727
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:24,000
Je suis épuisée. J'en peux plus.
I'm exhausted. I can't take it anymore.

728
00:43:24,080 --> 00:43:26,880
Et ces derniers kilos qui ne veulent pas partir.
And I can't shed those last few kilos.

729
00:43:27,400 --> 00:43:28,520
Ça va, maman ?
Are you okay, Mommy?

730
00:43:29,640 --> 00:43:31,440
Maman ne pleure pas vraiment.
Mommy's not really crying.

731
00:43:31,560 --> 00:43:33,040
Je répète, mon cœur.
I'm rehearsing, sweetie.

732
00:43:33,120 --> 00:43:36,711
Regarde, c'est du faux. Va jouer dans ta chambre.
Look, it's pretend crying. Go play in your room.

733
00:43:39,200 --> 00:43:40,800
Je les aime tellement.
I love them so much.

734
00:43:41,226 --> 00:43:42,640
Mais j'en peux plus.
But I can't take it anymore.

735
00:43:43,200 --> 00:43:46,320
Je suis là pour eux 24h/24, et ça ne semble jamais suffire.
I'm here for them 24/7,
but it never seems enough.

736
00:43:47,640 --> 00:43:49,280
Ça ne suffit jamais.
It never is enough.

737
00:43:50,800 --> 00:43:52,800
Comment on fait pour être un bon père ?
How do you be a good father?

738
00:43:55,360 --> 00:43:56,760
Je ne suis pas un bon père.
I'm not a good father.

739
00:44:03,640 --> 00:44:06,280
Qui veut une bonne nouvelle dans tout ce malheur ?
Who wants some good news
in all this misery?

740
00:44:06,720 --> 00:44:07,920
Sofia a eu le rôle.
Sofia got the part.

741
00:44:08,840 --> 00:44:11,040
Super ! Mais je le savais.
Great! But I knew it.

742
00:44:11,640 --> 00:44:14,880
Tu vois, dans ce petit monde fermé du cinéma français,
You see, in this closed little world
of French cinema,

743
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:17,360
il y a des réalisateurs assez malins
there are directors smart enough

744
00:44:17,480 --> 00:44:19,800
pour caster une femme noire dans un film en costume.
to cast a black woman in a costume drama.

745
00:44:19,880 --> 00:44:21,840
Non, Sofia joue l'esclave.
No, Sofia's playing the slave.

746
00:44:22,520 --> 00:44:25,640
-Non ! -Elle fait le ménage, elle évente la duchesse,
-No!
-She does the cleaning, fans the duchess,

747
00:44:25,720 --> 00:44:27,720
dort sur une paillasse...
sleeps on a straw mattress...

748
00:44:28,280 --> 00:44:30,160
Elle va m'en vouloir.
She'll scream at me.

749
00:44:30,720 --> 00:44:32,320
-Je suis l'esclave ? -Ouais.
-I'm the slave?
-Yeah.

750
00:44:33,120 --> 00:44:34,440
Avec des dialogues en plus.
With extra dialogue.

751
00:44:34,560 --> 00:44:37,000
J'ai eu le rôle ? Dans un film avec JoeyStarr !
I got the part?
In a movie with JoeyStarr!

752
00:44:37,960 --> 00:44:38,960
Putain !
Oh, fuck!

753
00:44:42,200 --> 00:44:43,440
Oh, Gabriel !
Oh, Gabriel!

754
00:44:43,520 --> 00:44:46,960
Je t'aime, je t'aime !
I love you, I love you!

755
00:44:59,480 --> 00:45:01,720
-Belle vue, non ? -Très.
-A nice view, huh?
-Very.

756
00:45:04,760 --> 00:45:06,640
Je ne couche pas avec Gabriel.
I'm not sleeping with Gabriel.

757
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:10,648
Tu devrais le lui dire, il a l'air de penser le contraire.
You should tell him,
he seems to think you are.

758
00:45:10,760 --> 00:45:11,680
Non, mais...
No, but...

759
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:16,000
On était là pour négocier des tarifs préférentiels pour nos acteurs.
We were there to negotiate special rates
for our actors.

760
00:45:16,120 --> 00:45:17,640
On vous a vus et...
We saw you and...

761
00:45:17,760 --> 00:45:21,680
L'envie subite de s'embrasser et de prendre une chambre ? Ça arrive.
Got the sudden urge to kiss
and get a room? It happens.

762
00:45:27,160 --> 00:45:29,200
Tu es très douée pour séduire les gens.
You're very good at seducing people.

763
00:45:29,960 --> 00:45:32,160
Cette fille avait raison. Tu es un monstre.
That girl was right. You're a monster.

764
00:45:35,680 --> 00:45:38,120
Bon... On faisait semblant.
Okay... We were pretending.

765
00:45:39,760 --> 00:45:41,800
On était là pour voir le directeur...
We were there to see the manager...

766
00:45:42,360 --> 00:45:45,360
pour parler de la chambre que Samuel gardait pour ses maîtresses.
to talk about the room
Samuel kept for his mistresses.

767
00:45:45,920 --> 00:45:47,960
On l'a appris hier.
We found out about it yesterday.

768
00:45:48,080 --> 00:45:51,880
On se demandait si on pouvait le faire passer en note de frais.
We wondered if we could pass it off
as a legitimate expense.

769
00:45:52,440 --> 00:45:55,280
On vous a vus arriver… et on a paniqué.
We saw you show up… and we panicked.

770
00:45:55,880 --> 00:45:58,880
-Dissimuler un abus de biens sociaux ? -Non...
-Covering up a misuse of company funds?
-No...

771
00:46:01,560 --> 00:46:02,480
Si.
Yes.

772
00:46:03,560 --> 00:46:06,280
On avait peur. De vous.
We were scared. Of you.

773
00:46:08,440 --> 00:46:10,231
Vous me tutoyez moins, maintenant.
Now you're being less familiar.

774
00:46:12,760 --> 00:46:14,808
Je ne sais pas comment me comporter avec vous.
I don't know how to behave around you.

775
00:46:40,640 --> 00:46:44,040
-Vous êtes sûre que c'est la seule solution ? -Faites-moi confiance, Audrey.
-Are you sure this is the only solution?
-Trust me, Audrey.

776
00:46:48,840 --> 00:46:51,320
Mesdames et messieurs, Mme Audrey Fleurot !
Ladies and gentlemen, Ms. Audrey Fleurot!

777
00:46:53,120 --> 00:46:55,960
Beyoncé a fait ça après son concert pour Kadhafi.
Beyoncé did this
after her concert for Gaddafi.

778
00:46:57,760 --> 00:47:01,240
Je veux vous dire combien je suis ravie d'être avec vous ce soir.
I want to tell you how delighted I am
to be with you tonight.

779
00:47:01,720 --> 00:47:04,880
Je n'ai pas besoin de vous dire à quel point les médias peuvent être cruels,
I don't need to tell you
how cruel the media can be,

780
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:07,280
à monter des histoires à partir de rien.
making a story out of nothing.

781
00:47:07,360 --> 00:47:09,920
C'est pourquoi je veux vous dire
This is why I want to tell you

782
00:47:10,040 --> 00:47:12,120
que je suis allé à cette soirée
that I went to that party

783
00:47:12,200 --> 00:47:16,040
uniquement pour mes enf... Uniquement pour les enfants...
purely for my ch...
Purely for the children...

784
00:47:16,440 --> 00:47:18,720
Pour les enfants du monde entier
For the children around the world

785
00:47:18,800 --> 00:47:20,520
qui souffrent de malnutrition,
suffering from malnutrition,

786
00:47:21,040 --> 00:47:23,680
d'un manque d'eau potable et de maladies.
a lack of clean drinking water
and disease.

787
00:47:24,200 --> 00:47:27,440
C'est pourquoi j'ai le plaisir de remettre...
This is why I'm delighted to hand over...

788
00:47:28,240 --> 00:47:30,200
la totalité de la somme
the entire amount

789
00:47:30,320 --> 00:47:33,840
que m'a versée M. Kadropov à l'UNICEF.
paid to me by Mr. Kadropov to UNICEF.

790
00:47:34,200 --> 00:47:40,346
La totalité de la somme, soit 10 000 euros. 20 000 euros, pardon. 20 000 euros.
The entire amount of 10,000 euros. 20,000 euros, sorry. 20,000 euros.

791
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:45,600
Merci.
Thank you.

792
00:47:52,400 --> 00:47:54,106
Vous avez oublié de signer.
You've forgotten to sign it.

793
00:47:55,520 --> 00:47:56,520
Pardon. Excusez-moi.
Sorry. Excuse me.

794
00:48:02,440 --> 00:48:03,280
Merci.
Thank you.

795
00:48:06,160 --> 00:48:08,080
Toujours aucune nouvelle de la nounou.
Still no news from the nanny.

796
00:48:08,160 --> 00:48:09,400
Vous en avez trouvé une ?
You found one?

797
00:48:09,960 --> 00:48:12,640
-Ouais. -Bien, j'ai peut-être un film pour toi.
-Yeah.
-Good, I may have a movie for you.

798
00:48:13,440 --> 00:48:14,400
Quoi ?
What?

799
00:48:14,520 --> 00:48:17,320
Michel Hazanavicius. Il t'a vu avec Kadropov.
Michel Hazanavicius.
He saw you with Kadropov.

800
00:48:17,440 --> 00:48:21,360
-Il te veut pour le prochain OSS 117. -Mathias, c'est super !
-He wants you for the next OSS 117.
-Mathias, that's great!

801
00:48:22,800 --> 00:48:24,560
Tu vas pouvoir payer tes impôts.
You'll be able to pay your taxes.

802
00:48:24,680 --> 00:48:27,720
Tu peux leur dire ? J'ai une phobie de l'administration.
Can you tell them?
I have an administration phobia.

803
00:48:27,840 --> 00:48:29,493
Je vais chercher du champagne.
I'll get some champagne.

804
00:48:33,520 --> 00:48:35,680
Fais une liste des acteurs de Mathias.
Make a list of Mathias's actors.

805
00:48:36,280 --> 00:48:40,680
On pourra peut-être en garder certains, même des grands noms, mais il faut faire vite.
We may be able to keep some,
even major names, but we have to be quick.

806
00:48:40,760 --> 00:48:41,960
Le salaud !
The bastard!

807
00:48:42,080 --> 00:48:44,120
On se vengera, t'inquiète pas.
We'll have our revenge, don't worry.

808
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:49,840
L'Allemand se retire.
The German's pulling out.

809
00:48:50,400 --> 00:48:51,240
Quoi ?
What?

810
00:48:51,320 --> 00:48:53,360
Il a appris que Mathias rejoint StarMédia.
He heard Mathias is going to StarMédia.

811
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:58,280
Il dit que sans lui, l'agence va perdre trop de valeur.
He says that without him,
the agency will lose too much value.

812
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:00,440
Tu en es sûr ?
Are you sure about this?

813
00:49:00,520 --> 00:49:03,040
-Je ne suis pas encore sénile ! -Mais ton ouïe...
-I'm not senile yet!
-But your hearing...

814
00:49:03,160 --> 00:49:05,440
Attends. Qu'est-ce qu'Hélène dit ?
Hang on. What does Hélène say?

815
00:49:05,520 --> 00:49:07,080
Elle est furieuse contre Mathias.
She's furious with Mathias.

816
00:49:07,640 --> 00:49:08,880
Il l'a fait exprès ?
Did he do it on purpose?

817
00:49:09,280 --> 00:49:13,000
On est débarrassés des Allemands, mais on ne vaut plus grand-chose.
So we're free of the Germans,
but we're not worth much.

818
00:49:13,120 --> 00:49:14,120
Je préfère ça.
I prefer that.

819
00:49:14,200 --> 00:49:16,400
-Et s'il l'avait fait exprès ? -Quoi ?
-What if he did it on purpose?
-What?

820
00:49:17,280 --> 00:49:19,440
Pour qu'on ne soit pas rachetés.
So we wouldn't be bought up.

821
00:49:20,320 --> 00:49:23,000
Un acte généreux de Mathias ? Quelle blague !
A generous act from Mathias? What a joke!

822
00:49:24,120 --> 00:49:26,720
Peut-être pas généreux, mais c'est un stratège.
Maybe not generous,
but he is a strategist.

823
00:49:29,480 --> 00:49:30,520
Quoi ?
What?

824
00:49:33,400 --> 00:49:34,520
L'idiot !
The idiot!

825
00:49:35,920 --> 00:49:37,320
Oui, l'idiot !
Yes, idiot!

826
00:49:43,040 --> 00:49:44,080
Il se retire ?
He's pulling out?

827
00:49:45,840 --> 00:49:49,040
Non, je n'ai pas dit à M. Hirsch que je rejoignais StarMédia.
No, I didn't tell Mr. Hirsch
I was going to StarMédia.

828
00:49:51,040 --> 00:49:53,040
Je ne sais pas comment il l'a appris.
I don't know how he found out.

829
00:49:54,280 --> 00:49:55,440
Hélène, calme-toi.
Hélène, calm down.

830
00:49:55,560 --> 00:49:57,120
Portes en cours d'ouverture.
Doors opening.

831
00:49:57,200 --> 00:49:59,600
-Je ne sais pas quoi dire... -Bravo, Mathias !
-I don't know what to say...
-Well done, Mathias!

832
00:50:00,200 --> 00:50:01,960
Laisse-moi digérer l'information...
Let me digest the information...

833
00:50:03,880 --> 00:50:06,924
Merci, Mathias. Je te rappelle.
Thank you, Mathias. I'll call you back.

834
00:50:07,120 --> 00:50:10,880
Mathias, bravo ! Laisse-moi t'embrasser.
Mathias, bravo! Let me kiss you.

835
00:50:13,160 --> 00:50:14,440
Super, Mathias !
Great, Mathias!

836
00:50:17,600 --> 00:50:18,960
Tu as fait quelque chose de formidable.
You did a wonderful thing.

837
00:50:20,280 --> 00:50:21,320
Bravo !
Bravo!

838
00:50:30,040 --> 00:50:31,640
-Champagne. -Champagne !
-Champagne.
-Champagne!

839
00:50:32,640 --> 00:50:35,480
Faire croire à tout le monde que tu allais chez nos rivaux
Making everyone think
you were going to our rivals

840
00:50:35,560 --> 00:50:38,160
pour sauver l'agence... Vivre dangereusement !
to save the agency... Living dangerously!

841
00:50:38,240 --> 00:50:40,000
Respect, M. Barneville !
Respect, Mr. Barneville!

842
00:50:41,040 --> 00:50:42,640
Le héros du jour !
The hero of the day!

843
00:50:42,720 --> 00:50:44,160
M. Barneville !
Mr. Barneville!

844
00:50:44,280 --> 00:50:46,720
Mathias, vous entrerez dans l'histoire.
Mathias, you'll go down in history.

845
00:50:51,800 --> 00:50:54,080
Désolé de vous avoir insulté.
Sorry I insulted you.

846
00:50:54,200 --> 00:50:55,760
Dîner demain ?
Dinner tomorrow?

847
00:50:56,320 --> 00:50:58,520
Jean Gabin aussi. Dis pardon, Jean Gabin.
Jean Gabin, too. Say sorry, Jean Gabin.

848
00:50:58,640 --> 00:51:00,520
-Laisse tomber. -Brave garçon !
-Forget it.
-Good boy!

849
00:51:00,640 --> 00:51:03,400
Mais quel idiot ! Pourquoi vous ne nous avez rien dit ?
But what an idiot! Why didn't you tell us?

850
00:51:03,520 --> 00:51:05,800
Je ne voulais prendre aucun risque.
I didn't want to take any risks.

851
00:51:07,760 --> 00:51:10,000
J'aurais tellement voulu que Samuel voie ça.
I just wish Samuel could see this.

852
00:51:11,440 --> 00:51:12,360
Encore une goutte.
Another drop.

853
00:51:12,440 --> 00:51:14,120
Vous n'alliez jamais partir ?
You were never going to leave?

854
00:51:14,240 --> 00:51:15,640
-Non ! -Vous en doutez ?
-No!
-Do you doubt it?

855
00:51:16,960 --> 00:51:18,560
Un peu. Mais c'est moi.
A bit. But that's me.

856
00:51:18,640 --> 00:51:19,920
Quel rabat-joie !
What a wet blanket!

857
00:51:21,320 --> 00:51:22,960
-On trinque ? -Oui !
-A toast?
-Yes!

858
00:51:23,040 --> 00:51:24,600
-À ASK ! -À ASK !
-To ASK!
-To ASK!

859
00:51:28,560 --> 00:51:29,560
Longue vie !
Long life!

860
00:51:32,480 --> 00:51:34,080
Il est bon, ce pétillant.
Good bubbly.

861
00:51:34,640 --> 00:51:35,840
Un peu jeune.
A bit young.
